    "id": "sS1psyud7AU",
    "title": "Introducing the Graduate School of Public Policy at The University of Tokyo",
    "channel": "東京大学 / The University of Tokyo",
    "channelId": "UCYI6VqtL5HFWdVhfD4oFPoA",
    "description": "The Graduate School of Public Policy at the University of Tokyo, abbreviated to GraSPP, has trained professionals in diverse fields of public policy by delivering an academic education that balances law, political science and economics, since its establishment in 2004. GraSPP is a highly diversified graduate school with students with nearly equal gender balance and various backgrounds. Our faculty members consist of academics, who provide intellectual foundations, and experienced policy practitioners, who share their first-hand professional knowledge and experience with students.\n\nOur two-year Master of Public Policy programs offer an extensive and diverse selection of courses. The MPP programs are designed for those who aspire to be globally competitive public policy practitioners equipped with academic theories, professional knowledge, and practical capacities. For more information, visit http://www.pp.u-tokyo.ac.jp/en/\n\n\n東京大学, The University of Tokyo, UTokyo, 公共政策大学院, 公共政策学教育部, Graduate School of Public Policy, GraSPP\n\n公共政策学教育部",
